<!--
    BM-005 — Scheduled Budget Alert Threshold Check
    ================================================

    Declares a single ``ir.cron`` record that periodically evaluates
    every confirmed budget line's consumption against the configured
    threshold percentages (75, 90, 100, 110) and creates
    ``budget.alert`` records for newly-crossed thresholds.

    R-06 Compliance
    ===============
    The scheduled evaluation is declared here as a data-file XML
    ``ir.cron`` record (NOT via a Python-level scheduler such as
    ``threading.Timer`` or ``APScheduler``). This is the canonical
    Odoo pattern and is mandated by AAP Rule R-06.

    Contract With ``budget.alert._cron_check_budget_alerts``
    ========================================================
    The ``code`` field invokes
    ``model._cron_check_budget_alerts()``. The method name MUST match
    exactly the ``@api.model`` method defined on ``budget.alert`` in
    ``models/budget_alert.py``. Renaming one side of this contract
    without renaming the other will cause the cron run to fail with
    ``AttributeError`` at invocation.

    Schedule
    ========
    Hourly evaluation (``interval_number=1``, ``interval_type='hours'``)
    satisfies the BM-005 performance target of < 1 hour alert
    detection latency after a threshold crossing occurs.

    The ``user_id`` is set to ``base.user_root`` so the cron runs with
    the superuser context needed to traverse every company's budgets
    (the multi-company ``ir.rule`` records in
    ``security/budget_security.xml`` would otherwise scope the search
    to the user's company list).

    Precedent
    =========
    Pattern mirrors ``addons/account/data/service_cron.xml``
    (e.g. ``ir_cron_account_move_send`` — also a ``state='code'`` cron
    with ``interval_type='days'`` that invokes a method on a business
    model, sets ``user_id`` to ``base.user_root``, and lives OUTSIDE
    any ``data noupdate`` wrapper so that upgrades re-apply the
    record).
-->
<odoo>
    <record id="ir_cron_budget_alert" model="ir.cron">
        <field name="name">Budget Management: Evaluate Alert Thresholds</field>
        <field name="model_id" ref="model_budget_alert"/>
        <field name="state">code</field>
        <field name="code">model._cron_check_budget_alerts()</field>
        <field name="user_id" ref="base.user_root"/>
        <field name="interval_number">1</field>
        <field name="interval_type">hours</field>
        <field name="active" eval="True"/>
    </record>
</odoo>
